-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 21 (COSTS), Divisions 2 to 6: rules 17 to 29 (procedure on assessment, the basis of assessment,
-- the certificate, review, interest).  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  Divisions 1's rules 1 to 16 are in
-- roc5-o21-general.l4, which imports this module (rule 1(2) points to rule 22); Appendix 1 (fixed costs) and
-- rule 10 are in roc5-o21-appendix.l4.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The last day of every period is O 3 r 3's answer (an input), never counted here.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 21, Division 2 -- Procedure on assessment`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 17 -- filing the bill of costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 21 r 17 the period for filing the bill of costs` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 12
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- "within 12 months after the date on which the entire cause or matter is finally disposed of, including any
-- appeals arising, unless the Court otherwise orders": the last day is the O 3 r 3 count from that date.
-- When the Court has ordered otherwise, the period no longer binds and the Court's order governs: not covered.
-- src:3037 | 17. A party entitled to have any costs assessed must file the bill of costs within 12 months after the date on which the entire cause or matter is finally disposed of, including any appeals arising, unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 17 (src:3037-3037)
GIVEN `the date the bill of costs is filed` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the Court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 17 the bill of costs is filed in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court has ordered otherwise`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the Court otherwise orders" and the order's terms are not in the Rules
        IF `the date the bill of costs is filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 12 months after the date on which the entire cause or matter is finally disposed of, including any appeals arising" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 18 -- notice of the time appointed for assessment`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 21 r 18 the notice period before the assessment` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- "at least 14 days' notice of the date and time appointed for assessment": the last day for giving the notice
-- is 14 days before the date appointed (O 3 r 3).  "Where the bill of costs has been filed in accordance with
-- Rule 17" is a "where" condition.
-- src:3039 | 18. Where the bill of costs has been filed in accordance with Rule 17, the Registrar must give to the party beginning the proceedings at least 14 days’ notice of the date and time appointed for assessment.
@ref O 21 r 18 (src:3039-3039)
GIVEN `the bill of costs has been filed in accordance with Rule 17` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Registrar gives the notice` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 18 the Registrar's notice of the assessment is given in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bill of costs has been filed in accordance with Rule 17`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the bill of costs has been filed in accordance with Rule 17" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `the date the Registrar gives the notice` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 14 days’ notice of the date and time appointed for assessment" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 19 -- delivery of bills`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 21 r 19(1) the period for sending a copy of the bill of costs` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 2
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:3041 | 19. —(1) A party whose costs are to be assessed in any assessment proceedings must, within 2 days after receiving a notice of the date and time under Rule 18, send a copy of the party’s bill of costs to every other party entitled to be heard in the proceedings. (2) Notice need not be given to any party who has not filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest or taken any part in the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings.
@ref O 21 r 19(1) (src:3041-3041)
GIVEN `the date the copy of the bill of costs is sent to every other party entitled to be heard` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 19(1) the copy of the bill of costs is sent in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the copy of the bill of costs is sent to every other party entitled to be heard` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 2 days after receiving a notice of the date and time under Rule 18" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- (2): "Notice need not be given to any party who has not filed and served a notice of intention to contest or
-- not contest or taken any part in the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings."
-- src:3041 | 19. —(1) A party whose costs are to be assessed in any assessment proceedings must, within 2 days after receiving a notice of the date and time under Rule 18, send a copy of the party’s bill of costs to every other party entitled to be heard in the proceedings. (2) Notice need not be given to any party who has not filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest or taken any part in the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings.
@ref O 21 r 19(2) (src:3041-3041)
GIVEN `the party has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has taken part in the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 19(2) notice need not be given to the party` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the party has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest`) AND (NOT `the party has taken part in the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any party who has not filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest or taken any part in the proceedings"

-- (3): "Paragraph (2) does not apply where an order for the assessment of a solicitor's bill of costs made under
-- the Legal Profession Act, at the application of the solicitor, gave rise to the assessment proceedings."
