@ref O 21 r 19(3) (src:3042-3042)
GIVEN `an order for the assessment of a solicitor's bill of costs made under the Legal Profession Act at the application of the solicitor gave rise to the assessment proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 19(3) paragraph (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `an order for the assessment of a solicitor's bill of costs made under the Legal Profession Act at the application of the solicitor gave rise to the assessment proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) does not apply where an order for the assessment of a solicitor’s bill of costs made under the Legal Profession Act, at the application of the solicitor, gave rise to the assessment proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (3) says where paragraph (2) does not apply and does not say that it does apply anywhere else

