§§ `Rule 20 -- form of bill of costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3044 | 20. —(1) Every bill of costs must set out in 3 separate sections the following: ( a )
-- src:3045 | work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs;
-- src:3046 | ( b )
-- src:3047 | work done for and in the assessment of costs;
-- src:3048 | ( c )
-- src:3049 | all disbursements made in the cause or matter.
@ref O 21 r 20(1) (src:3044-3049)
GIVEN `it sets out work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out work done for and in the assessment of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out all disbursements made in the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the three are in separate sections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 20(1) the bill of costs has the three separate sections` MEANS
    IF `it sets out work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs`
       AND `it sets out work done for and in the assessment of costs`
       AND `it sets out all disbursements made in the cause or matter`
       AND `the three are in separate sections`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every bill of costs must set out in 3 separate sections the following"

-- src:3050 | (2) The costs claimed for paragraph (1)( a ) and ( b ) must be indicated as one global sum for each section, while the costs claimed for paragraph (1)( c ) must set out the sum claimed for each item of disbursement.
