GIVEN `the costs for work done in the cause or matter are one global sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs for work done in the assessment of costs are one global sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum for each item of disbursement is set out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 20(2) the costs are indicated as the rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the costs for work done in the cause or matter are one global sum`
       AND `the costs for work done in the assessment of costs are one global sum`
       AND `the sum for each item of disbursement is set out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be indicated as one global sum for each section, while the costs claimed for paragraph (1)( c ) must set out the sum claimed for each item of disbursement"

