-- (6): for contentious business, (a) to (d) are musts; (e) "may" and (f) is an inclusion, so neither is a
-- condition of compliance.  Where the assessment is not for contentious business the paragraph does not speak.
-- src:3054 | (6) For assessment of costs for contentious business — ( a )
-- src:3055 | the bill of costs must set out sufficient information that will enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2), and must comply with any requirements specified in the practice directions;
-- src:3056 | ( b )
