@ref O 21 r 20(6) (src:3054-3065)
GIVEN `the assessment is for contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out sufficient information to enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2) and complies with the requirements in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where attendances, telephone conversations and correspondence are concerned, it states the number of each and, where possible, the total hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where costs have already been awarded for any of the events set out, it indicates this fact and the amount awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains a succinct narrative of the legal and factual issues involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 20(6) the bill of costs for contentious business has the content the rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the assessment is for contentious business`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For assessment of costs for contentious business" [for read as where: assumed, not ruled, recorded as a fork in NOTES.md]
        IF `it sets out sufficient information to enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2) and complies with the requirements in the practice directions`
           AND `where attendances, telephone conversations and correspondence are concerned, it states the number of each and, where possible, the total hours`
           AND `where costs have already been awarded for any of the events set out, it indicates this fact and the amount awarded`
           AND `it contains a succinct narrative of the legal and factual issues involved`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the bill of costs must set out sufficient information that will enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2)"

-- (6)(e): the bill "may also contain the lists of authorities cited".  A permission, inside the same "For assessment
