    IF `the assessment is for contentious business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For assessment of costs for contentious business" [for read as where: assumed, not ruled, recorded as a fork in NOTES.md]

-- (6)(f): "work done in the cause or matter includes work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement".
-- Work on negotiating a settlement is within the first section of the bill (paragraph (1)(a)).  The word is
-- "includes", so the list of what else counts is not closed.
