      `the work is work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 20(6)(f) the work is work done in the cause or matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the assessment is for contentious business`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For assessment of costs for contentious business" [for read as where: assumed, not ruled, recorded as a fork in NOTES.md]
        IF `the work is work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "work done in the cause or matter includes work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement" and the list of what else counts is not closed

