§§ `Rule 21 -- powers of the Registrar assessing costs payable out of a fund`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3067 | 21. —(1) Where any costs are to be paid out of a fund, the Registrar may give directions as to the parties who are entitled to attend on the assessment of those costs and may disallow the costs of attendance of any party not entitled to attend by virtue of the directions and whose attendance the Registrar considers unnecessary. (2) Where the Court has directed that a solicitor’s bill of costs be assessed for the purpose of being paid out of a fund, the Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks fit, adjourn the assessment for a reasonable period and direct the solicitor to send to any person having an interest in the fund a copy of the bill, or any part of the bill, free of charge together with a letter containing the following information: ( a )
@ref O 21 r 21(1) (src:3067-3067)
GIVEN `the costs are to be paid out of a fund` IS A BOOLEAN
