    IF `the costs are to be paid out of a fund` AND `the party is not entitled to attend by virtue of the Registrar's directions` AND `the Registrar considers the party's attendance unnecessary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may disallow the costs of attendance of any party not entitled to attend by virtue of the directions and whose attendance the Registrar considers unnecessary"

