-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 21, Division 3 -- Assessment of costs`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 22 -- basis of assessment`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The two bases the rule names; the Rules define "standard basis" and "indemnity basis" by paragraphs (2) and (3).
DECLARE `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 22(2) the standard basis`
    `o 21 r 22(3) the indemnity basis`
    `o 21 r 22 another basis`

-- What the order for costs says about the basis.
DECLARE `o 21 r 22(4) what the order for assessment says about the basis` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates no basis`
    `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates the standard basis`
    `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates the indemnity basis`
    `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates a basis other than the standard basis or the indemnity basis`

-- Whose side a doubt is resolved for.
DECLARE `o 21 r 22 side` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 22 the paying party`
    `o 21 r 22 the receiving party`

-- (1): the amount allowed on the standard basis, "unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order
-- costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis".  The result is an enum, so there is a yes/no twin below.
-- src:3075 | 22. —(1) Subject to the other provisions of these Rules, the amount of costs which any party is entitled to recover is the amount allowed after assessment on the standard basis where — ( a )
-- src:3076 | an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings;
-- src:3077 | ( b )
-- src:3078 | an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund; or
-- src:3079 | ( c )
-- src:3080 | no order for costs is required,
-- src:3081 | unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis.
@ref O 21 r 22(1) (src:3075-3081)
GIVEN `an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no order for costs is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
`o 21 r 22(1) the basis on which the amount of costs is allowed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` OR `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` OR `no order for costs is required`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where — ( a ) an order is made ...; ( b ) an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund; or ( c ) no order for costs is required"
        IF `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Court then orders the indemnity basis; paragraph (1) says only that the standard basis is not the basis
        OTHERWISE JUST `o 21 r 22(2) the standard basis`

-- src:3075 | 22. —(1) Subject to the other provisions of these Rules, the amount of costs which any party is entitled to recover is the amount allowed after assessment on the standard basis where — ( a )
-- src:3076 | an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings;
-- src:3077 | ( b )
-- src:3078 | an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund; or
-- src:3079 | ( c )
-- src:3080 | no order for costs is required,
-- src:3081 | unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis.
@ref O 21 r 22(1) (src:3075-3081)
GIVEN `an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no order for costs is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 22(1) the amount of costs is the amount allowed after assessment on the standard basis` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` OR `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` OR `no order for costs is required`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where — ( a ) an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings; ( b ) an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund; or ( c ) no order for costs is required" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1), the indemnity basis: is the assessment on the indemnity basis?  Paragraph (1) names the indemnity basis
-- only in its "unless": it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on that basis.
-- The Rules do not say when it so appears, and an order is the Court's own act, so the function takes the order as
-- a fact (fork F7).  Where the Court has ordered the indemnity basis the answer is yes; where it has not, and the
-- text puts the costs on the standard basis, the answer is no.
-- src:3075 | 22. —(1) Subject to the other provisions of these Rules, the amount of costs which any party is entitled to recover is the amount allowed after assessment on the standard basis where — ( a )
-- src:3076 | an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings;
-- src:3077 | ( b )
-- src:3078 | an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund; or
-- src:3079 | ( c )
-- src:3080 | no order for costs is required,
-- src:3081 | unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis.
@ref O 21 r 22(1) (src:3075-3081)
GIVEN `an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no order for costs is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered the costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 22(1) the costs are assessed on the indemnity basis` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court has ordered the costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis" and whether the Court then orders it is the Court's act, not the Rules'
        IF NOT (`an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` OR `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` OR `no order for costs is required`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) speaks of the standard basis in the three cases it lists and of the indemnity basis only in its "unless"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text puts the costs on the other basis): "is the amount allowed after assessment on the standard basis" [the standard basis excludes the indemnity basis: assumed, not ruled, fork F7]

-- (2): on the standard basis "a reasonable amount in respect of all costs reasonably incurred is to be allowed";
-- doubts as to whether the costs were reasonably incurred or reasonable in amount "are to be resolved in favour
-- of the paying party".  A cost that was not reasonably incurred, or not reasonable in amount, is not said to
-- be disallowed in so many words.
-- src:3082 | (2) On an assessment of costs on the standard basis, a reasonable amount in respect of all costs reasonably incurred is to be allowed, and any doubts which the Registrar may have as to whether the costs were reasonably incurred or were reasonable in amount are to be resolved in favour of the paying party; and in these Rules, the term “the standard basis”, in relation to the assessment of costs, is to be construed accordingly.
@ref O 21 r 22(2) (src:3082-3082)
GIVEN `the cost was reasonably incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is a reasonable amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 22(2) the amount is allowed on the standard basis` MEANS
    IF `the cost was reasonably incurred` AND `the amount is a reasonable amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a reasonable amount in respect of all costs reasonably incurred is to be allowed"

-- src:3082 | (2) On an assessment of costs on the standard basis, a reasonable amount in respect of all costs reasonably incurred is to be allowed, and any doubts which the Registrar may have as to whether the costs were reasonably incurred or were reasonable in amount are to be resolved in favour of the paying party; and in these Rules, the term “the standard basis”, in relation to the assessment of costs, is to be construed accordingly.
@ref O 21 r 22(2) (src:3082-3082)
GIVEN basis IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 r 22 side`
`o 21 r 22 in whose favour the doubts of the Registrar are resolved` MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `o 21 r 22(2) the standard basis` THEN JUST `o 21 r 22 the paying party`
    WHEN `o 21 r 22(3) the indemnity basis` THEN JUST `o 21 r 22 the receiving party`
    WHEN `o 21 r 22 another basis` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (2) and (3) speak of the standard basis and the indemnity basis only

-- "the standard basis" in these Rules is construed as paragraph (2) describes.
-- src:3082 | (2) On an assessment of costs on the standard basis, a reasonable amount in respect of all costs reasonably incurred is to be allowed, and any doubts which the Registrar may have as to whether the costs were reasonably incurred or were reasonable in amount are to be resolved in favour of the paying party; and in these Rules, the term “the standard basis”, in relation to the assessment of costs, is to be construed accordingly.
