GIVEN basis IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 22(2) the basis is the standard basis` MEANS
    IF basis EQUALS `o 21 r 22(2) the standard basis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in these Rules, the term “the standard basis”, in relation to the assessment of costs, is to be construed accordingly"

-- (3): on the indemnity basis "all costs are to be allowed except insofar as they are of an unreasonable amount
