-- (4): an order for assessment that indicates no basis, or a basis other than the standard or the indemnity
-- basis, means assessment on the standard basis.  An order that names one of the two says what it says.
-- src:3084 | (4) Where the Court makes an order for assessment of costs without indicating the basis of assessment or on any basis other than the standard basis or the indemnity basis, the costs are to be assessed on the standard basis.
