    WHEN `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates the standard basis` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (4) speaks only of an order that gives no basis or another basis
    WHEN `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates the indemnity basis` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (4) speaks only of an order that gives no basis or another basis

-- (4), the indemnity basis: an order that itself indicates the indemnity basis puts the costs on it; an order that
-- indicates no basis, another basis or the standard basis does not (fork F7).
-- src:3084 | (4) Where the Court makes an order for assessment of costs without indicating the basis of assessment or on any basis other than the standard basis or the indemnity basis, the costs are to be assessed on the standard basis.
