    WHEN `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates no basis` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text puts the costs on the other basis): "the costs are to be assessed on the standard basis" [the standard basis excludes the indemnity basis: assumed, not ruled, fork F7]
    WHEN `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates a basis other than the standard basis or the indemnity basis` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text puts the costs on the other basis): "the costs are to be assessed on the standard basis" [the standard basis excludes the indemnity basis: assumed, not ruled, fork F7]
    WHEN `o 21 r 22(4) it indicates the standard basis` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text names the two bases as alternatives): "any basis other than the standard basis or the indemnity basis" [the standard basis excludes the indemnity basis: assumed, not ruled, fork F7]

-- (5): "Despite paragraphs (1) to (4), if any action is brought in the General Division, which would have been
-- within the jurisdiction of a State Court, the claimant is not entitled to any more costs than the claimant
-- would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court, unless the General
-- Division otherwise orders."
-- src:3085 | (5) Despite paragraphs (1) to (4), if any action is brought in the General Division, which would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court, the claimant is not entitled to any more costs than the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court, unless the General Division otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 22(5) (src:3085-3085)
GIVEN `the action is brought in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 22(5) the claimant is entitled to more costs than in a State Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the action is brought in the General Division` AND `it would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if any action is brought in the General Division, which would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court"
        IF `the General Division has ordered otherwise`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the General Division otherwise orders" and the order's terms are not in the Rules
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant is not entitled to any more costs than the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court"

-- The most the claimant may recover, where the cap applies: the lesser of the costs allowed and the costs that
-- would have been allowed in a State Court.  A number, so there is a yes/no twin above and this one answers
-- NOTHING where the cap does not apply.
-- src:3085 | (5) Despite paragraphs (1) to (4), if any action is brought in the General Division, which would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court, the claimant is not entitled to any more costs than the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court, unless the General Division otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 22(5) (src:3085-3085)
GIVEN `the costs allowed after assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court` IS A NUMBER
      `the action is brought in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 21 r 22(5) the most costs the claimant may recover` MEANS
    IF `the action is brought in the General Division` AND `it would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court` AND (NOT `the General Division has ordered otherwise`)
    THEN JUST (IF `the costs allowed after assessment` AT MOST `the costs the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court` THEN `the costs allowed after assessment` ELSE `the costs the claimant would have been entitled to if the proceedings had been brought in a State Court`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the cap is for "an action brought in the General Division, which would have been within the jurisdiction of a State Court" and yields to "unless the General Division otherwise orders"

