-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 25 and 26 -- the certificate`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "When the bill of costs has been assessed, the solicitor must apply for the certificate of the Registrar for
-- the amount of costs allowed": "when" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).  The rule states no time.
-- src:3103 | 25. When the bill of costs has been assessed, the solicitor must apply for the certificate of the Registrar for the amount of costs allowed by the Registrar.
@ref O 21 r 25 (src:3103-3103)
GIVEN `the bill of costs has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 25 the solicitor must apply for the certificate of the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the bill of costs has been assessed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the bill of costs has been assessed" [when counts as where: delegated-definitions ruling (c) of 2026-11-05]

-- src:3105 | 26. Upon the assessment of the bill of costs, the certificate of the Registrar, unless set aside, is conclusive as to the amount of costs allowed, and, where the order contains a submission to pay, the solicitor may after 48 hours, if there is no application for review, apply for an enforcement order to be issued in respect of the costs allowed.
@ref O 21 r 26 (src:3105-3105)
GIVEN `the certificate has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 26 the certificate is conclusive as to the amount of costs allowed` MEANS
    IF `the certificate has been set aside`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the certificate of the Registrar, unless set aside, is conclusive as to the amount of costs allowed"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "where the order contains a submission to pay, the solicitor may after 48 hours, if there is no application
-- for review, apply for an enforcement order": 48 hours after the assessment.  The hours that have run are
-- what the person can state.
-- src:3105 | 26. Upon the assessment of the bill of costs, the certificate of the Registrar, unless set aside, is conclusive as to the amount of costs allowed, and, where the order contains a submission to pay, the solicitor may after 48 hours, if there is no application for review, apply for an enforcement order to be issued in respect of the costs allowed.
@ref O 21 r 26 (src:3105-3105)
GIVEN `the order contains a submission to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours that have run since the assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `there is an application for review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 26 the solicitor may apply for an enforcement order for the costs allowed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order contains a submission to pay`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the order contains a submission to pay" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `the hours that have run since the assessment` AT MOST 48
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the solicitor may after 48 hours" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]
        IF `there is an application for review`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is no application for review"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 27 -- application to a Judge for review`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): a party to the assessment proceedings who is dissatisfied with the Registrar's decision on an item may
-- apply to a Judge to review the assessment as to that item or part of an item.
-- src:3108 | 27. —(1) Any party to any assessment proceedings who is dissatisfied with the decision of the Registrar in respect of any item may apply to a Judge to review the assessment as to that item or part of an item, as the case may be. (2) An application under this Rule for review of the Registrar’s decision may be made at any time within 14 days after that decision.
@ref O 21 r 27(1) (src:3108-3108)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the assessment proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is dissatisfied with the decision of the Registrar in respect of an item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 27(1) the party may apply to a Judge to review the assessment as to the item` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to the assessment proceedings` AND `the person is dissatisfied with the decision of the Registrar in respect of an item`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any party to any assessment proceedings who is dissatisfied with the decision of the Registrar in respect of any item may apply to a Judge"

`o 21 r 27(2) the period for applying for review` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:3108 | 27. —(1) Any party to any assessment proceedings who is dissatisfied with the decision of the Registrar in respect of any item may apply to a Judge to review the assessment as to that item or part of an item, as the case may be. (2) An application under this Rule for review of the Registrar’s decision may be made at any time within 14 days after that decision.
@ref O 21 r 27(2) (src:3108-3108)
GIVEN `the date the application for review is made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 27(2) the application for review is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the application for review is made` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made at any time within 14 days after that decision" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- (3): "by summons and ... heard in chambers, unless the Judge otherwise orders".
-- src:3109 | (3) An application under this Rule must be made by summons and must be heard in chambers, unless the Judge otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 27(3) (src:3109-3109)
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Judge has ordered that it be heard other than in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 27(3) the application is made and heard as the rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made by summons`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under this Rule must be made by summons"
        IF `the Judge has ordered that it be heard other than in chambers`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the Judge otherwise orders" and the Judge's order is not in the Rules
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the application for review of an item does not prejudice the Registrar's power under Rule 14 to issue an
-- interim certificate for the items not under review.
-- src:3110 | (4) An application under this Rule for review of the Registrar’s decision in respect of any item does not prejudice the power of the Registrar under Rule 14 to issue an interim certificate in respect of the items of the Registrar’s decision which are not the subject of the review.
@ref O 21 r 27(4) (src:3110-3110)
GIVEN `the item is not the subject of the review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 27(4) the application for review prejudices the Registrar's power to issue an interim certificate for the item` MEANS
    IF `the item is not the subject of the review`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prejudice the power of the Registrar under Rule 14 to issue an interim certificate in respect of the items of the Registrar’s decision which are not the subject of the review"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of the items that are not under review

-- (5): "Judge" in Rules 27 and 28.  The definition says what "Judge" "means", and a "means" closes the list: the
-- Registrar is not a Judge for Rules 27 and 28 (so Rule 27(1) applies to a Judge, to whom the Registrar's
-- decision is taken for review).  Order 1 rule 3 defines "Judge" differently, adds a Magistrate and the Registrar
-- "in cases where he or she is empowered to act", and is not encoded here; it is not mixed in (fork F9).
DECLARE `o 21 r 27(5) who sits` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 27(5) a Judge sitting in the General Division`
    `o 21 r 27(5) a District Judge`
    `o 21 r 27(5) a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`
    `o 21 r 27(5) the Registrar`
    `o 21 r 27(5) any other person`

-- src:3111 | (5) In this Rule and Rule 28, “Judge” means a Judge sitting in the General Division or a District Judge and includes a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate.
@ref O 21 r 27(5) term Judge (src:3111-3111)
GIVEN who IS A `o 21 r 27(5) who sits`
      `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 27(5) a person is a Judge in Rules 27 and 28` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `o 21 r 27(5) a Judge sitting in the General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 27(5) a District Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 27(5) a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` THEN
        IF `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "includes a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate"
    WHEN `o 21 r 27(5) the Registrar` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Judge” means a Judge sitting in the General Division or a District Judge and includes a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate" [means closes the list: assumed, not ruled, fork F9]
    WHEN `o 21 r 27(5) any other person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Judge” means a Judge sitting in the General Division or a District Judge and includes a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate" [means closes the list: assumed, not ruled, fork F9]

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 28 -- review of the Registrar's decision by the Judge`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3113 | 28. —(1) Unless the Judge otherwise directs, no further evidence may be received on the hearing of the review of the Registrar’s decision by the Judge, but except as mentioned, on the hearing of the review, the Judge may exercise all such powers and discretion as are vested in the Registrar in relation to the subject matter of the application. (2) At the conclusion of the review, the Judge may make such order as the circumstances require, and in particular may order the Registrar’s certificate to be amended or (except where the dispute as to the item under review is as to amount only) order the item to be remitted to the Registrar for assessment.
@ref O 21 r 28(1) (src:3113-3113)
GIVEN `the Judge has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 28(1) further evidence may be received on the hearing of the review` MEANS
    IF `the Judge has otherwise directed`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless the Judge otherwise directs" and the direction is not in the Rules
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no further evidence may be received on the hearing of the review of the Registrar’s decision by the Judge"

-- src:3113 | 28. —(1) Unless the Judge otherwise directs, no further evidence may be received on the hearing of the review of the Registrar’s decision by the Judge, but except as mentioned, on the hearing of the review, the Judge may exercise all such powers and discretion as are vested in the Registrar in relation to the subject matter of the application. (2) At the conclusion of the review, the Judge may make such order as the circumstances require, and in particular may order the Registrar’s certificate to be amended or (except where the dispute as to the item under review is as to amount only) order the item to be remitted to the Registrar for assessment.
@ref O 21 r 28(2) (src:3113-3113)
GIVEN `the dispute as to the item under review is as to amount only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 28(2) the Judge may order the item to be remitted to the Registrar for assessment` MEANS
    IF `the dispute as to the item under review is as to amount only`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(except where the dispute as to the item under review is as to amount only) order the item to be remitted to the Registrar for assessment"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 21, Division 6 -- Interest`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 29 -- interest on costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 21 r 29(1) type of costs` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 29(1)(a) assessed costs`
    `o 21 r 29(1)(b) costs fixed by the Court`
    `o 21 r 29(1)(c) costs agreed between the parties`
    `o 21 r 29(1)(d) costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order`
    `o 21 r 29(2) costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order`
    `o 21 r 29 other costs`

`o 21 r 29(1) the rate of interest per year` MEANS 5.33%

-- The table in paragraph (1): the commencement date of each type of costs.
-- src:3116 | 29. —(1) The costs mentioned in the first column of the following table carry interest at 5.33% per year from the date mentioned in the second column of the table until payment: First column
-- src:3117 | Second column
-- src:3118 | Type of costs
-- src:3119 | Commencement date
-- src:3120 | ( a )
-- src:3121 | assessed costs
-- src:3122 | Date of assessment
-- src:3123 | ( b )
-- src:3124 | costs fixed by the Court
-- src:3125 | Date of order
-- src:3126 | ( c )
-- src:3127 | costs agreed between the parties
-- src:3128 | Date of agreement
-- src:3129 | ( d )
-- src:3130 | costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order
-- src:3131 | Date of judgment.
@ref O 21 r 29(1) (src:3116-3131)
GIVEN type IS A `o 21 r 29(1) type of costs`
      `the date of assessment` IS A DATE
      `the date of the order` IS A DATE
      `the date of the agreement` IS A DATE
      `the date of judgment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 21 r 29(1) the date from which the costs carry interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER type
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(a) assessed costs` THEN JUST `the date of assessment`
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(b) costs fixed by the Court` THEN JUST `the date of the order`
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(c) costs agreed between the parties` THEN JUST `the date of the agreement`
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(d) costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN JUST `the date of judgment`
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(2) costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (2) says Part 4 costs do not carry interest, so there is no commencement date
    WHEN `o 21 r 29 other costs` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the table names four types of costs and no more

-- The yes/no twin of the date (the result is a date, which cannot carry a "no").
-- src:3116 | 29. —(1) The costs mentioned in the first column of the following table carry interest at 5.33% per year from the date mentioned in the second column of the table until payment: First column
-- src:3117 | Second column
-- src:3118 | Type of costs
-- src:3119 | Commencement date
-- src:3120 | ( a )
-- src:3121 | assessed costs
-- src:3122 | Date of assessment
-- src:3123 | ( b )
-- src:3124 | costs fixed by the Court
-- src:3125 | Date of order
-- src:3126 | ( c )
-- src:3127 | costs agreed between the parties
-- src:3128 | Date of agreement
-- src:3129 | ( d )
-- src:3130 | costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order
-- src:3131 | Date of judgment.
-- src:3132 | (2) Costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order do not carry any interest.
@ref O 21 r 29 (src:3116-3132)
GIVEN type IS A `o 21 r 29(1) type of costs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 29 the costs carry interest at the rate of 5.33% per year` MEANS
    CONSIDER type
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(a) assessed costs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(b) costs fixed by the Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(c) costs agreed between the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(d) costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(2) costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order do not carry any interest."
    WHEN `o 21 r 29 other costs` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the table names four types of costs and no more

-- The interest on an amount of costs for ONE year: the amount times the rate.  The text says "5.33% per year ... until
-- payment" and nothing about simple or compound interest or about a part of a year, so the function gives the
-- one amount on which every such reading agrees (fork F8).  A sum, so there is a yes/no twin above.
-- src:3116 | 29. —(1) The costs mentioned in the first column of the following table carry interest at 5.33% per year from the date mentioned in the second column of the table until payment: First column
-- src:3117 | Second column
-- src:3118 | Type of costs
-- src:3119 | Commencement date
-- src:3120 | ( a )
-- src:3121 | assessed costs
-- src:3122 | Date of assessment
-- src:3123 | ( b )
-- src:3124 | costs fixed by the Court
-- src:3125 | Date of order
-- src:3126 | ( c )
-- src:3127 | costs agreed between the parties
-- src:3128 | Date of agreement
-- src:3129 | ( d )
-- src:3130 | costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order
-- src:3131 | Date of judgment.
-- src:3132 | (2) Costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order do not carry any interest.
@ref O 21 r 29(1) (src:3116-3132)
GIVEN type IS A `o 21 r 29(1) type of costs`
      `the amount of the costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 21 r 29(1) the interest on the costs for one year` MEANS
    CONSIDER type
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(a) assessed costs` THEN JUST (`the amount of the costs` TIMES `o 21 r 29(1) the rate of interest per year`)
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(b) costs fixed by the Court` THEN JUST (`the amount of the costs` TIMES `o 21 r 29(1) the rate of interest per year`)
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(c) costs agreed between the parties` THEN JUST (`the amount of the costs` TIMES `o 21 r 29(1) the rate of interest per year`)
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(1)(d) costs under Parts 1, 2 and 3 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN JUST (`the amount of the costs` TIMES `o 21 r 29(1) the rate of interest per year`)
    WHEN `o 21 r 29(2) costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a sum cannot carry the no): "Costs under Part 4 of Appendix 1 to this Order do not carry any interest." and the yes/no twin answers JUST FALSE
    WHEN `o 21 r 29 other costs` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the table names four types of costs and no more

-- Whether a given day is within the period of interest: from the commencement date "until payment".
-- src:3116 | 29. —(1) The costs mentioned in the first column of the following table carry interest at 5.33% per year from the date mentioned in the second column of the table until payment: First column
@ref O 21 r 29(1) (src:3116-3116)
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 29(1) interest is running on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the commencement date`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the date mentioned in the second column of the table until payment" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]
        IF `the day of payment` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the day of payment`
                  WHEN JUST paid THEN
                      IF `the day asked about` AT MOST paid
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until payment" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the day of payment is not given
